From 8ce7be8d9682e29b2e2b5fda2f98ce3d50ac2109 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Micha=C5=82=20Iwanicki?= <michal.iwanicki@3mdeb.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:06:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/28] Revert "feat(rdv3): use SFCP PSA call instead of RSE
 comms"
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This reverts commit 66e46af64f0c15ee2ddb22fda39df836c6ec1937.

The RD-V3 FVP stack of RD-INFRA-2025.07.03 runs a TF-M RSE that accepts
only the RSE comms protocol versions 0 and 1 and rejects SFCP messages.
Upstream SFCP_SUPPORT_LEGACY_MSG_PROTOCOL calls sfcp_convert_to_legacy_*
functions that no source defines, so it gives no compatible mode.

Go back to rse_comms over MHUv3 for the AP to RSE PSA calls. The FIRME
attestation hooks added after the SFCP switch (7953d9aec) call the RSE
through psa_call(), which both transports implement. Their use over
rse_comms is untested. Keep the MECID width hook added to rdv3_common.c
after the switch, and keep the upstream GIC init in bl31_plat_arch_setup().

Drop this patch once the RSE runs a TF-M release with SFCP support.

Signed-off-by: Michał Iwanicki <michal.iwanicki@3mdeb.com>
